Subject: SOP Multi-Target Semantic Compiler Purpose Plan

Description: Dependency plan following bounded purpose signature. It preserves the implementation frontier and prevents the canonical purpose from masquerading as completed compiler work.

@ [plan_uuid] 7026575a-f8e3-422b-950b-d1b9157b390d
@ [source_snapshot_uuid] a90af861-ccb4-433f-964d-eff53d7457ad
@ [plan_status] designed_not_activated

& [Phase_0_PurposeAuthority] is current
  + preserve source and SJS artifacts
  + sign only the language purpose, roles, logical compiler contract, and future proof obligations
  + release no implementation

& [Phase_1_ProfileSources] requires new preserved source
  + specify one minimal verbose, condensed, and machine LanguageProfile
  + specify minimum standard modules and exact serialization
  + specify compiler and runtime ABI encodings
  + define bootstrap and independent verifier identities
  + [activation] separate source, SJS, feature support, and implementation slice

& [Phase_2_MinimumFrontEnd] depends_on Phase_1
  + implement source generation, parser, source map, role closure, name resolution, kinds, types, relations, contracts, effects, diagnostics, and canonical SemanticIR serialization
  + keep all effects and provider calls absent
  + [proof] positive and negative pure fixtures

& [Phase_3_MinimumTargets] depends_on Phase_2
  + implement SOP-X exact projection for the pure fixture
  + implement SOP-N blueprint emission without provider execution
  + implement SOP-H exact admission over a supplied mock neural proposal
  + emit correspondence, loss, diagnostics, and proof bundle

& [Phase_4_IndependentConformance] depends_on Phase_3
  + run expected SemanticIR and observations through an independent checker or hand-authored oracle
  + compare verbose, condensed, and machine surface roots
  + test instruction-shaped data, hidden effect, unsupported feature, stale dependency, and neural abstention
  + [release_gate] no wider target claim until fixture evidence passes

& [Phase_5_CantorIntegration] depends_on Phase_4 and separate feature source
  + connect proof-carrying query to source and SemanticIR identities
  + evaluate exact, lexical, graph, vector, and learned routing under measured benchmarks
  + keep learned routing subordinate to signed record retrieval

& [Phase_6_AdvancedTargets] is requirement-gated
  + provider-backed neural compilation
  + shared-inference tool adapters
  + workflow and operator-shell projection
  + FPGA interpreter or native synthesis
  + every target requires separate source, profile, owner, proof, compatibility, rollback, and measured benefit

& [PlanStopConditions] are mandatory
  + missing profile authority
  + source or dependency drift
  + role leakage
  + SemanticIR ambiguity
  + hidden effect or authority
  + unsupported target feature
  + inability to produce independent expected result
  + neural output promoted beyond declared proposal grade
  + target work without signed benefit

& [CurrentPlanAuthority] is absent
  + this plan orders future work but does not assign, implement, execute, train, deploy, call a provider, or synthesize hardware
